 "rules": {
  "R1": "E73-F10's ROI fundamental (0.01 Hz) is at least 3 SE from zero with sign-flip p <= 0.01, and its board fundamental at least 5 SE. Otherwise the 0.01 Hz point is reported as a non-detection and R3/R4 are not scored.",
  "R2": "the three 0.05 Hz reference blocks' |H| agree with a straight line in time within 3 SE each; that line is what every ratio to 0.05 Hz is taken against, and its slope is the session's gain drift.",
  "R3": "the heat path is low-pass: |H(0.025)|/|H_ref(0.05)| > 1 and |H(0.01)|/|H_ref(0.05)| > |H(0.025)|/|H_ref(0.05)|, each by at least 1 SE. A flat or falling ratio refutes the picture E63 built.",
  "R4": "the discriminator, which has no PASS: the measured lag at 0.01 Hz is compared with M1's 42.6 deg and M2's 26.4 deg, and the surviving model is named. Both may fail.",
  "R5": "0.05 Hz, measured twice over: E73-F10's fifth harmonic agrees with the reference line's H(0.05) within 3 SE of the complex difference.",
  "R6": "hold: at least 95% of the in-launch telemetry samples of every block's analysed laps read 790 MHz or more, and the block's die mean stays under 65 C. The per-launch one-second dips are counted and reported WITHOUT a verdict, which is E63's lesson: a per-launch gate fails on the governor's idle-reset dip at any load.",
  "inclusion": "a transfer point enters the across-frequency fit only when its board amplitude is at least 5 SE; otherwise the ratio's denominator is unstable. Points that fail it are published with their errors and left out of the fit."
 }
